# CI/CD & Integrations homework (ДЗ)

When the user prompt refers to **шаг N** of CI/CD ДЗ, **CI/CD**, **OAuth2**, **аналитика**, **платежи**, **мониторинг**, **security audit** for this homework, or **cicd_integrations_documentation**:

## Deliverables per step

1. **Execute** the step scope (pipeline, audit, OAuth, analytics, payments, monitoring, logging, tests, docs as requested).
2. **`cicd_integrations_documentation.md`** (root) — update in the **same work cycle**:
   - Architecture / CI / Security / OAuth / Analytics / Payments / Monitoring / Logging — when that area changes
   - §9 AI process — prompts, techniques, problems/solutions for this step
   - §10 Journal — always: step row, Issue link, status
3. **GitHub Issue** — one Issue per DZ step (or update epic [#37](https://github.com/Sintik1/Qa_Asistant/issues/37)); comment with decisions and commit SHAs.
4. **`development_report.md`** — add/update journal row + short pointer: «CI/CD ДЗ шаг N → `cicd_integrations_documentation.md` §10».

## Still mandatory (`.cursorrules` §10–11)

Do **not** skip Issues or `development_report.md`. `cicd_integrations_documentation.md` is **additional** (submission artifact), not a replacement. Backend ДЗ artifact `backend_documentation.md` stays separate — update it only if a step changes Backend API/deploy contracts.

## All other project rules stay in force

- Architecture: thin routes, Repository + UoW, no string-built SQL, secrets in `.env` only
- New logic → Pytest / Vitest as applicable
- User gate: do not mark a DZ step done without user OK when the plan requires it
- Git: commit/push only when the user explicitly asks
- **Do not add new MCP servers without explicit user approval**

## Skills

Use as applicable: `qa-assistant-process` (always), `qa-assistant-backend`, `qa-assistant-api`, `qa-assistant-testing`, `qa-assistant-ui`, `qa-assistant-react`.

## Before final reply for a DZ step

- [ ] Issue created/updated
- [ ] `cicd_integrations_documentation.md` updated (§10 at minimum)
- [ ] `development_report.md` updated (journal + link)
- [ ] User reply: Issue link + docs mentioned
